# Q4 2026 Earnings Call

**Alex, Chief Executive**  
1 October 2026 to 16 October 2026

## Highlights

| | |
|---|---:|
| Opening index | 96.00 |
| Closing index | 90.84 |
| Change | −5.16 (−5.37%) |
| Quarter range | 88.50 to 101.25 |
| Enough Threshold | 105.00 |
| Threshold revisions | 4 |
| Positions held | 1 |


## Prepared Remarks

**Operator**

Welcome to the Q4 2026 results call for Alex. Following prepared remarks, we will open the line for questions from analysts. I will now turn the call over to the Chief Executive, Alex.

**Alex, Chief Executive**

Thank you, and thanks to everyone for being with us today.

The Personal Standing Index opened the quarter at 96.00 and closed at 90.84, a change of −5.16 points, or −5.37%. This was a challenging quarter, and the result reflects conditions across the peer set rather than any change in our underlying fundamentals.

The Enough Threshold was adjusted 4 times in the period, and now stands at 105.00. I would characterize that as a sign of the strength of the market.

I won't pretend the quarter was without challenges. Performance in sourdough starter age, parallel parking under observation and hairline trajectory was below our expectations.

For the coming quarter, we are prioritizing sourdough starter age. We are also undertaking a strategic review of procedural competence, and we will update you as appropriate.

Across the peer set, Dana (DANA) posted a gain of 6.48 points. We congratulate them, and we are studying their results carefully.

The peer set expanded during the quarter with the addition of your manager's manager.

The Standard Classification was extended during the quarter to include cat's apparent affection, now reflected in our results.

Operator, we are now ready to take questions.

## Question-and-Answer Session

**Operator**

Our first question comes from the line of an analyst at Continental Research Partners. Please go ahead.

**Analyst, Continental Research Partners**

Thanks for taking the question. Could you speak to performance in sourdough starter age? It looks like Dana has widened their lead there.

**Alex, Chief Executive**

I'd point you to the long-term trend.

**Operator**

We will take our next question from Second Street Equities.

**Analyst, Second Street Equities**

I wanted to ask about parallel parking under observation. Marcus Bell appears to be well ahead. Is that structural?

**Alex, Chief Executive**

We see that as a timing issue.

**Operator**

The next question is from Regional Securities. Your line is open.

**Analyst, Regional Securities**

Can you give us any guidance on the timeline for reaching the Enough Threshold? The shortfall is currently 14.16.

**Alex, Chief Executive**

We don't break that out.

**Operator**

Our next question comes from Independent Research Associates. Please go ahead.

**Analyst, Independent Research Associates**

Could you comment on the performance of Dana? A gain of 6.48 points seems significant.

**Alex, Chief Executive**

We'll have more to say about that next quarter.

**Operator**

We will take our next question from General Brokerage Services.

**Analyst, General Brokerage Services**

You currently hold one position. Can you talk about your strategy there?

**Alex, Chief Executive**

I'd caution against reading too much into a single quarter.

**Operator**

The next question is from Provincial Capital Markets. Your line is open.

**Analyst, Provincial Capital Markets**

Can you comment on the Spotlight readings this quarter?

**Alex, Chief Executive**

That's something we're looking at very closely.

**Operator**

That concludes our question-and-answer session. I will turn the call back to Alex for any closing remarks.

**Alex, Chief Executive**

Thank you all for your questions. We look forward to speaking with you next quarter.

**Operator**

Ladies and gentlemen, that concludes today's call. You may now disconnect.


